WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.190
Why I reviewed my car insurance
policy and why you should too.

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:06.650
Hi I'm Wil Alexander an injury attorney.

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:09.290
I want to tell you a story about myself.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:11.870
When I first started
practicing injury law,

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:15.830
I didn't realize a lot about
my own personal car insurance.

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:20.120
So what I quickly realized was there's
these different coverages out there that

00:00:20.121 --> 00:00:23.150
people really don't know about.
So most people think, oh,

00:00:23.151 --> 00:00:27.800
I'll get car insurance when
I get my license, I have
to have it, it's state law,

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:33.010
got to have car insurance - so in case
I hit someone else that they can recover

00:00:33.051 --> 00:00:36.860
from that for the property damage
or for potentially an injury claim.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:42.130
But what I didn't realize was that I
had the opportunity to purchase what's

00:00:42.261 --> 00:00:44.240
called Underinsured Motorist Coverage.

00:00:44.241 --> 00:00:48.050
So there's different coverages out there
that you can talk with your insurance

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.040
agent about,

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:54.460
about getting car insurance that can
protect you from if someone else hits you.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:56.570
So there's MedPay coverage,

00:00:56.781 --> 00:01:00.230
there is underinsured motorist coverage,

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.710
there's uninsured motorist
coverage, which you have to have,

00:01:03.711 --> 00:01:07.730
but this underinsured coverage
I really didn't know about.

00:01:07.731 --> 00:01:09.320
And what that does is,

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:13.610
let's say that I'm driving down the road
and someone hits me that has minimum

00:01:13.611 --> 00:01:18.200
state limits. So in South
Carolina, that's a 25/50 policy.

00:01:18.201 --> 00:01:23.201
So that means that I can only recover
$25,000 from the at-fault person.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:27.260
But if I have this
Underinsured Motorist Coverage,

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:32.680
I could collect off of my own insurance
to take back what was taken from me and

00:01:33.711 --> 00:01:38.711
to pay my medical bills pay for lost
wages and other damages that I had because

00:01:40.581 --> 00:01:44.330
someone hit me in a wreck.
So it's something that you
really should think about.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:45.860
Most people, again,

00:01:45.861 --> 00:01:50.660
I think they only think about well I
get car insurance to protect if I hit

00:01:50.661 --> 00:01:51.470
someone else.

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:55.100
But there are these different coverages
out there that can protect you,

00:01:55.400 --> 00:02:00.400
your own insurance that can protect you
and your family if someone hits you when

00:02:01.131 --> 00:02:04.130
you're driving down the road and
they don't have adequate insurance.

00:02:04.131 --> 00:02:09.131
So I'd really encourage you to reach
out to me if you'd like for me to review

00:02:09.441 --> 00:02:12.680
your policy. I'd love to do that.
Let you know what coverages you have.

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:17.300
Your insurance agent definitely talk
with them and understand what these

00:02:17.301 --> 00:02:19.340
different coverages are
because importantly,

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:22.370
if you don't have that coverage
and you get in a wreck,

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:25.430
you can't then go get it. It's
either you have it or you don't.

00:02:25.431 --> 00:02:28.670
So it's something that you need to
think about to protect yourself,

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:30.230
to protect your family,

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:34.340
and something that a lot of people I
think really overlook that they don't

00:02:34.341 --> 00:02:35.001
understand.

00:02:35.001 --> 00:02:40.001
And even I really did not understand it
until I got into the personal injury law

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:44.840
practice. So really encourage you to look
into that. If you have any questions,

00:02:44.841 --> 00:02:47.780
feel free to shoot me an
email, text our number,

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:49.220
any way you can reach out to me.

00:02:49.221 --> 00:02:51.830
I'd be glad to answer any
questions that you have.

